desc(
	mode: "source",
	language: "general",
	title: "Template Autoescape Off",
	title_zh: "检测到Template Autoescape Off",
	type: vuln,
	level: middle,
	rule_id: "source-insecure-api-template-autoescape-off",
	risk: "Security",
	desc: <<<DESC
Migrated from Semgrep rule `template-autoescape-off` (/tmp/semgrep-rules/python/django/security/audit/xss/template-autoescape-off.yaml).
Original message: Detected a template block where autoescaping is explicitly disabled with '{% autoescape off %}'. This allows rendering of raw HTML in this segment. Turn autoescaping on to prevent cross-site scripting (XSS). If you must do this, consider instead, using `mark_safe` in Python code.

CWE: CWE-79: Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation ('Cross-site Scripting')
References:
- https://docs.djangoproject.com/en/3.1/ref/templates/builtins/#autoescape
DESC,
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
Review the flagged code and follow the framework's secure coding guidance: use safe APIs, escape output, and avoid hardcoded credentials.
SOLUTION,
	alert_min: 1,
	"file://pos.html": <<<POS
{% 	 	 
 	 
	autoescape		off



%}

POS,
	"safefile://neg.sample": <<<NEG
# safe sample
no secrets here
just regular code
NEG,
)

${*.html}.pattern_regex(/{%\s+autoescape\s+off\s+%}/) as $p0
$p0 as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "middle",
	title: "Template Autoescape Off",
	title_zh: "检测到Template Autoescape Off",
	message: "Template Autoescape Off",
}
